.SS "\fBVARIABLE_FLAG\fP csmp::intToVARIABLE_FLAG (int i)"

.PP
variable flag Options numbered in this sequence, starting with zero are: PLAIN, ANY, INIT_GUESS, INIT_COND, FIELD_DATA, PERIODIC, DIRICH, NEUMANN, ROBIN, CONSTANT_FLUX 
.SS "string csmp::parse (\fBManifoldType\fP topology)"

.PP
converts classifiers to strings so that they can be printed STAND_ALONE, ///< multiplicated point SPLIT_BOUNDARY, ///< 2-node manifold along a \fBSplitBoundary\fP (most common) SPLIT_BOUNDARY_CROSSING, ///< 4-node manifold intersection of split boundaries MULTI_SB_CROSSING, ///< 6-node cross of 3 SBs in SPLIT_BOUNDARY_TERMINATION, ///< T-intersection of SBs are termination of SB against \fBBoundary\fP SPLIT_BOUNDARY_END, ///< termination against model boundary

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
if the split boundary cannot be determined, method returns SPLIT_BOUNDARY 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBVARIABLE_FLAG\fP csmp::parseCondition (std::string & s)"
Interprets the supplied string as an essential (boundary) condition\&. Possible values are given in '\fBCSMP_definitions\&.h\fP' and MULTIPLE\&. The last type can be used to specify Cauchy or Robbin conditions\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The string that shall be interpreted as boundary condition\&. 
